# Design system

Mood Taster looks like a well-set page, not a dashboard. Two tones, flat fills,
and generous space do all the work. If a change needs a line or a gradient to
read clearly, the spacing or the type is wrong.

## Palette: two tones and one accent

| Token | Value | Role |
|-------|-------|------|
| `--ink` | `#14110f` | Tone 1. Every surface. |
| `--paper` | `#f2ebe0` | Tone 2. Every piece of content. |
| `--accent` | `#e4a01a` | Saffron. Small marks only. |

Every neutral in the UI is a **mix of the two tones**, never a new hue:

```css
--paper-muted: color-mix(in srgb, var(--paper) 72%, var(--ink));
--paper-quiet: color-mix(in srgb, var(--paper) 45%, var(--ink));
--ink-raised:  color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 92%, var(--paper));
```

Accent rules:

- Saffron is for **small marks**: eyebrows, step numbers, one emphasis per section
- It must never fill a surface, a button, or any large area. Roughly 1% of a
  viewport's painted area is the ceiling
- Never introduce a fourth hue. No zest, no status greens, no semantic reds.
  Failure and success read through copy, weight, and placement

## Never

- **No gradients.** No `linear-gradient`, `radial-gradient`, `conic-gradient`,
  color washes, blurred blooms, or tinted overlays. Solid fills only
- **No borders as decoration.** No hairline dividers, no `border-top` section
  rules, no outlined cards, no stroked circles or rings
- **No box shadows.** Depth is not a substitute for a border
- **No card grids** built out of boxes. Group with space and alignment
- **No `border-radius` above `2px`.** Prefer `0`

## Instead: separate with space and tone

Reach for these, in order:

1. **Space.** A section break is `--space-8`, not a 1px line
2. **Type.** Size, weight, and family carry hierarchy
3. **Tone.** Step a surface to `--ink-raised`, or invert to paper-on-ink, when a
   region genuinely needs to detach

Primary actions **invert the tones**: paper background, ink text. That is the
only "filled" element in the system.

## Spacing scale

Use the ramp; do not invent one-off values.

```css
--space-1: 0.25rem;  --space-5: 2rem;
--space-2: 0.5rem;   --space-6: 3rem;
--space-3: 0.75rem;  --space-7: 4rem;
--space-4: 1rem;     --space-8: clamp(4rem, 12vh, 7rem);
```

Section padding uses `--space-8` on the block axis and the shared page inset on
the inline axis. Related items sit `--space-4` apart; unrelated groups sit
`--space-6` or more apart. When something feels cramped, add space before adding
a divider.

## Required exceptions

These are accessibility features, not decoration, and must survive:

- `:focus-visible` outlines: keep a visible 2px focus ring on every interactive
  element. Never set `outline: none` without an equivalent replacement
- `box-sizing: border-box`
- Underlines on inline text links
- The `.grain` overlay: monochrome noise, no hue and no gradient. It is brand
  texture, not a substitute for structure. Do not add a second texture

## Sponsored placements

The Strategy doc (`/strategy`) requires paid placements to be unmistakably
labeled. Under this system, that label is **type, not a badge box**:

- Use an accent eyebrow, `Sponsored match`, in the same style as `.eyebrow`
- Never build a bordered pill, tinted chip, or shadowed card to carry it
- Never make the sponsored label quieter than the organic one it sits beside

## Motion

Entrance `rise` only, and one shared `--ease`. No spinning, pulsing, or looping
ambient animation. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.

## Checklist before shipping UI

- [ ] No gradient, border, or shadow added
- [ ] Any new color is `--ink`, `--paper`, `--accent`, or a mix of the first two
- [ ] Accent used only as a small mark
- [ ] Spacing values come from the ramp
- [ ] Focus states still visible on keyboard nav
